Ladybird captures the whole viewport for an element screenshot, and
draws the region starting at the element’s rectangle from it.

Gecko’s capture.canvas() draws the window from the rectangle’s left and
top coordinates, through drawWindow() or drawSnapshot(). ChromeDriver’s
ExecuteElementScreenshot() gets the element’s rect and captures with it
as the clip, and WebKit’s Session::takeScreenshot() passes the element
to a capture that clips to it as well.
